  "description": "Pat Callanan Property Sales Ltd. are delighted to bring Copperbeech House to the open market for sale by private treaty. Ideally positioned on the Athenry Road, within walking distance of Loughrea town centre and local shopping amenities, Copperbeech House is a substantial detached. Set in an established and convenient location, this unique property offers excellent versatility and significant potential for a purchaser seeking a spacious family home, dual-living accommodation or an investment opportunity, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nLoughrea is a vibrant and well-established town with a wide range of amenities on its doorstep. The town offers an excellent selection of shops, cafÃ©s, restaurants, schools, sporting facilities and everyday services, while the beautiful Loughrea Lake provides a wonderful natural amenity for walking, recreation and enjoying the outdoors.\nThe town is particularly well located for commuters, with convenient access to the M6 motorway, providing connectivity towards Galway city and the wider Midlands and Dublin. Galway city is readily accessible, while nearby towns including Athenry and Oranmore further enhance the property's appeal. For families, Loughrea offers a strong choice of primary and secondary schools, childcare facilities, sports clubs and community amenities, making it an attractive location for those looking to enjoy the benefits of town living while remaining within easy reach of Galway city.\n\nThe property is currently arranged as two separate accommodation units, providing considerable flexibility for a new owner. The main house accommodation comprises an entrance hall, living room, family room, kitchen, dining room, downstairs bedroom and shower room at ground floor level. Upstairs, there are a further four bedrooms, including one bedroom with ensuite and another with a separate WC, together with the main family bathroom. To the left-hand side of the property is a self-contained accommodation unit, converted from a former commercial space. This unit comprises a living room, kitchen, shower room, two bedrooms and a bathroom.\nThe property is heated by a combination of oil-fired central heating, a solid-fuel stove and fireplace. Externally, there is a detached garage to the rear together with generous off-street parking to the front.\n\n\nCopperbeech House represents an exciting opportunity to acquire a sizeable detached property in a highly convenient Loughrea location. The existing configuration offers a range of possibilities, whether as a substantial family home with additional accommodation, a multi-generational living arrangement or, subject to the relevant planning permissions, potential conversion into separate residential units.\nWith its generous floor area, detached nature, existing accommodation and proximity to the amenities of Loughrea town, the property offers considerable scope for those looking to create a home or investment tailored to their requirements.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the space, location and potential this distinctive property has to offer.\n\nAccommodation : \n\nEntrance Hall 2.11m x 4.58m 6.92ft x 15.03ft\nCarpet to floor\n\nFamily Room 3.33m x 3.58m 10.93ft x 11.75ft\nCarpet to floor\n\nLiving Room 3.80m x 6.52m 12.47ft x 21.39ft\nCarpet to floor, open fireplace\n\nKitchen 6.16m x 2.90m 20.21ft x 9.51ft\nTiles to floor, fitted kitchen units\n\nDining Room 3.24m x 3.09m 10.63ft x 10.14ft\nCarpet to floor, solid fuel stove\n\nDownstairs Bedroom 3.53m x 3.07m 11.58ft x 10.07ft\nCarpet to floor, sink in room\n\nShower Room 1.41m x 1.82m 4.63ft x 5.97ft\nTiles to floor and walls\n\nLanding 4.90m x 2.15m 16.08ft x 7.05ft\nCarpet to floor \n\nBedroom 2 3.83m x 2.76m 12.57ft x 9.06ft\nCarpet to floor\n\nEn-Suite 2 0.80m x 2.54m 2.62ft x 8.33ft\nTiles to floor and walls, electric shower \n\nBedroom 3 3.60m x 3.35m 11.81ft x 10.99ft\nCarpet to floor, corner sink\n\nBedroom 4 3.55m x 3.07m 1